# Publishing __EXT_NAME__ to Browser Stores

`.github/workflows/release.yml` builds Chrome + Firefox, creates a GitHub
release with both zips, and submits to both stores — triggered by a
`package.json` version bump pushed to main (no bump = no release).

## Credentials — mostly shared across your extensions

The store credentials are tied to your **developer accounts**, not individual
extensions, so you reuse most of them:

| Secret | Scope | Per-extension? |
|--------|-------|----------------|
| `CWS_CLIENT_ID` / `CWS_CLIENT_SECRET` / `CWS_REFRESH_TOKEN` | Google/CWS account | **No** — reuse |
| `CWS_EXTENSION_ID` | one CWS item | **Yes** |
| `AMO_JWT_ISSUER` / `AMO_JWT_SECRET` | Mozilla account API key | **No** — reuse |
| gecko id (`browser_specific_settings.gecko.id` in `manifest.firefox.json`) | one AMO listing | **Yes** (in code, not a secret) |

`~/.claude/scripts/setup-extension-publishing.sh` copies the 5 shared secrets
from `~/.local/share/secrets/browser-store-creds.env` and prompts for the new
`CWS_EXTENSION_ID`.

## One-time per developer account

**Chrome (do once, then reuse forever):**
1. [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/) → enable **Chrome Web Store API**.
2. Create an **OAuth client ID** (Web application), authorized redirect URI `https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground`.
3. **Publish the OAuth consent screen to "In production"** — Google Auth Platform → **Audience** → **Publish app**. Skipping this expires the refresh token every 7 days (`Invalid grant` failures).
4. Mint a refresh token at [OAuth Playground](https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground) (gear → use own creds → scope `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chromewebstore` → Authorize → Exchange).

**Firefox (do once, then reuse forever):**
- Generate a JWT issuer + secret at the [AMO API Key page](https://addons.mozilla.org/en-US/developers/addon/api/key/). This is the only place these exist — not recoverable once lost.

## Per new extension
1. Create the CWS item + AMO listing (first version usually uploaded manually).
2. Set a unique `browser_specific_settings.gecko.id` in `manifest.firefox.json` (publish-firefox.js hard-exits without it) — before the first push.
3. Run `~/.claude/scripts/setup-extension-publishing.sh <repo-dir> <ext-name>` — it copies the files, patches package.json, runs `npm install` to sync the lockfile, and sets the secrets.
4. Ensure `build:chrome` / `build:firefox` npm scripts exist (the workflow runs them).
5. Bump `package.json` version → push to main. CI does the rest.

## Notes
- CWS step uses full `publish:chrome` (upload + submit for review) with `continue-on-error` (CWS rejects uploads during a pending review). Switch to `publish:chrome:upload` for a manual submit gate.
- Both stores still gate on their own review (Chrome 1–3 days, Firefox often same-day). "Done" = submitted, not live.
- Manual re-publish without a version bump: `gh release delete vX.Y.Z --cleanup-tag --yes` then `gh workflow run release.yml --ref main`. A second dispatch after success double-submits AMO (version-exists) — for a Chrome-only retry, run `publish:chrome` locally against the zip.
